  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "9eXWGZSkUsIquYDE9C+w9NV+Qkw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:11:47.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Proposed at the Aug 14 weekly (00:25:08\u201300:32:23): implement document embedding the way Speckle embeds models into Notion.\n\nMechanism: the **Iframely protocol** provides metadata and standardized rules for embedding web content. A user copy-pastes a Powerhouse document URL into Notion, Miro, or SharePoint and gets a **live, interactive document editor** embedded in place.\n\nWhy it matters strategically: network-based organizations \u2014 the norm in construction \u2014 have different stakeholders on varied, entrenched systems. Embedding lets Powerhouse enter those workflows with almost no friction and supports organic growth, rather than demanding a platform switch. It converts every third-party wiki page or board into a potential Powerhouse surface.\n\nNext step from the meeting: integrate iframe embedding capabilities into the Datab project demo.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T18:11:47.243782+00:00"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:11:47.000Z"
    }
  },
